      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Although we have \"streamer mode\" now, which auto-declines friend requests, I would like to have this feature as a separate thing. I would use the streamer mode just for the auto-declining, but that mode also blocks stuff I want to see like thumbnails, pictures, and messages.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-30T16:47:32.696Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the Social Tab, we could have a \"Social Options\" sub-tap like we do with \"Advanced Settings\" under Settings and \"Performance Options\" under Safety.\n\nIt'd give us an option much like Discord already has in its \"Privacy & Safety\" user settings.\n\nWho to allow friend requests from:\n- Everyone\n- Friends of friends\n- Same world\n\nIt could work the same way as Discord's does where deselecting \"Friends of friends\" or \"Same world\" will automatically also deselect \"Everyone\" while selecting \"Everyone\" will also auto-select the other two options.\n\nSome people already know ahead of time whether or not they're wanting random friend requests, so this would be nice to have.\n\nThis also provides a solution to the problem of unwanted friend request spam Bryan Bortz mentioned for another suggestion.\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/dont-show-friends-in-someone-elses-friends-only-world-as-being-in-a-private-worl",
